        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tool-policy-audit): use truncateUtf16Safe for audit field truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe tool policy audit logger uses naive `.slice(0, MAX_AUDIT_FIELD_LENGTH)` to truncate field values. This can split surrogate pairs mid-character, producing garbled output in audit logs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace with `truncateUtf16Safe()` which preserves surrogate pair boundaries, matching the pattern used across the rest of the codebase (e.g. #101535, #101527, #101534, #102395, #102378).\n\n## Files Changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/agents/tool-policy-audit.ts` | +1 import, 1 line: `.slice(0,N)` → `truncateUtf16Safe()` |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
